{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01085 - MONDO_6875",
  "verbalization": "Pilocarpine is associated with Ocular Hypertension through a chain of indications and off-label uses. The drug is indicated for Open-angle Glaucoma, a condition that is also linked to Ocular Hypertension, suggesting a potential indirect relationship. The evidence is supported by the use of Pilocarpine in treating Open-angle Glaucoma, which is often associated with elevated intraocular pressure, a key driver of Ocular Hypertension. Additionally, off-label use of Apraclonidine and Latanoprostene Bunod, both indicated for Open-angle Glaucoma, is linked to Ocular Hypertension, reinforcing the possibility of a mechanistic or clinical connection. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role of Pilocarpine in the pathophysiology of Ocular Hypertension through its involvement in glaucoma management.",
